<h1>Study Spanish Guatemala</h1>
<p>&nbsp;Living with a Guatemalan family offers a unique and immersive experience that significantly aids in learning and understanding Spanish, according to Colin Pfening, a student from Whitworth University in Spokane, Washington. Having studied Spanish since he was eight years old and continuing through high school, Pfening decided to study for three weeks at Casa Xelajú in Quetzaltenango, Guatemala, driven by a personal sense of direction and a desire to explore Central American culture.</p>
