<p>&nbsp;The educational program at Casa Xelajú is structured into distinct components designed to maximize language acquisition. The curriculum is divided into grammar lessons covering conjugation, speaking, and writing, alongside conversation sessions focused on specific topics to build vocabulary and improve fluency. The instruction is highly personalized compared to traditional university settings, featuring intimate class sizes tailored to individual student preferences, with patient and supportive teachers who keep academic and language goals at the forefront.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Beyond formal classroom instruction, living with a Guatemalan family provides a realistic, everyday environment that helps students grasp the informal aspects of the Spanish language. This immersive lifestyle is further enriched by various cultural activities organized through the program, such as dance lessons, cooking lessons like making empanadas, and trips outside of Quetzaltenango for canopy tours and swimming.</p>
<p>&nbsp;Reflecting on his time in Guatemala, Pfening notes that the skills and cultural insights he gained will greatly benefit his professional life and future career. He describes Quetzaltenango as a wonderful city that fosters independence while allowing students to build meaningful connections with peers and teachers.</p>
